    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d116-a3">

                <pb facs="0317" n="287" sameAs="frus:frus1949v01/pg287"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Subenclosure 2]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of Defense</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Forrestal</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Executive Secretary of the National Security
                        Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Souers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-26">26 March 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Airfield Construction (NSC 45)</p>
                <p>In reply to your memorandum of 23 March 1949,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d116-f1"/>
                    requesting, pursuant to NSC Action 197, the
                    views of the Joint Chiefs of Staff with respect to NSC 45, I wish to inform you that the Joint Chiefs of Staff agree
                    that the development of the four airfields in the United Kingdom and the one
                    airfield in the Cairo–Suez area is in the national interest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James Forrestal</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
